comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T22:30:37.097Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict3117-item all-status corpus without omissions; request-specific history/index/tampering search and full live pm-up22, pm-7vr9 and pm-o2kc reads. Existing drift-scan cache and history verification owners are delivered; no event-index integrity owner exists. Original GH1593 report retained verbatim. Intake only, open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-25T23:02:06.817Z","harness:codex","Review clarification: the retained GitHub report is source evidence, not a prescribed cache algorithm. A last-record hash or partial prefix check alone cannot detect arbitrary same-length edits to earlier records. Cache validity must cover the complete authoritative history content through a full-file content digest or authoritative chain verification. Strict reads must verify every affected authoritative chain. Include a negative control that changes an earlier record without altering file length or the final record/hash, in both a warm process and after restart. Preserve the original report wording and keep implementation queued and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-25T23:41:18.600Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: content-sensitive authoritative stream validation for event-index reads plus explicit SDK verification receipts, bundled with isolated linked-test receipt verification under the related integrity work. Complete strict all-status census3118 read without omissions; no open PRs or security/dependency/secret alerts. Existing closed history repair and index-contention work remains delivered."
  "2026-10-25T23:57:39.770Z","harness:codex","Pre-fix regression proof executed in an independent temporary worktree at unchanged main3ba042b3d with isolated PM roots: the new history-event controls fail on stale same-length non-tail content and absent authoritative verification contracts. Related linked receipt controls also fail without source-index binding. Current focused suite passes48 cases; existing concurrent-writer/read snapshots remain nonblocking. Exact sealed timestamp preservation and caller-copy isolation were added before full coverage. Full-source coverage and public contract snapshots are being verified; no final gate result is claimed yet."
  "2026-10-26T00:22:46.033Z","harness:codex","First full verification ran11433 tests over1241seconds:861 files passed;13 assertions in7 files exposed contract/layout or environment issues rather than the new integrity behavior. Fixed exact flag allowance and shortened help within its407-token ceiling, preserved absent adapter options, and moved new tests below the unchanged120-file directory cap. Packed continuation resolves the host bundled npm through a command-local NODE_PATH; no global host configuration changed. All89 targeted regressions now pass, including actual MCP verification and the previously timed-out calibration entrypoint at15.5seconds. Full exact coverage is rerun with failure reporting enabled and without competing heavy lint/typecheck processes."
  "2026-10-26T01:12:49.014Z","harness:codex","Validation: complete quality:static pipeline passed, including exact contracts, dependency/advisory checks, CodeFactor complexity, SDK budgets, tracker assurances and mutation testing. Typecheck passed. Native controls cover source and snapshot authority, staged and custom roots, inherited Git selectors, missing/corrupted proof, sealed timestamps and same-length earlier history changes. Final canonical coverage and packed delivery checks follow before closure."
  "2026-10-26T01:39:44.245Z","harness:codex","Final complete source coverage passed: statements71014/71014, branches54642/54642, functions14608/14608, lines67183/67183; zero uncovered counts and no threshold/denominator changes. Full static pipeline, TypeScript targets, linked regressions and9 packed npx/bunx workflows passed. Published2026.10.25 consumer acceptance passed npm and Bun installed-agent sessions plus CLI/MCP transports. Latest pm-changelog is2026.10.25; package-owned regeneration follows closure. Required Sentry/telemetry gate previously passed with0 unresolved issues, fresh pm.command span metadata, exact settled command pairing and drained broker; historical release/nightly limitations remain with canonical owners."
  "2026-10-26T04:05:13.770Z","harness:codex","PR1596 review triage: accept exact-byte receipts for parseable invalid UTF-8, remove recorded-entry leakage from unverified fallback reads, and reduce concurrent whole-file reads. Two tracker findings are declined after live full reads: the new pm-j8z6 command is an intentionally failing reproduction on an open item, and the CLI-authored pm-0trehk text contains zero comma delimiters and decodes completely. Only this history-integrity item is reopened for source edits; receipt implementation remains closed."
  "2026-10-26T04:33:42.548Z","harness:codex","PR1596 review refinement proof: the three targeted regressions fail against unchanged ddc2d5ce1 in an isolated worktree. Current native suite passes 95 tests across five files; TypeScript targets and source static-quality detail pass. Public readHistorySnapshot now retains raw_bytes from the same read while raw/entries parsing stays unchanged. Unverified fallback projections discard strict-only recorded entries and content validation limits whole-file read fan-out to32. Two tracker findings are declined using native TOON decoding and intentional open-item reproduction semantics."
  "2026-10-26T05:21:04.561Z","harness:codex","PR1596 final review delivery: 136 linked history/SDK/CLI/MCP tests pass; 95 focused review regressions pass including three controls that fail on unchanged reviewed head. TypeScript, source static quality, contracts, dependency policy, tracker context/graph/integrity and mutation gates pass across the recorded canonical stages. Review fixes retain exact original bytes, stable unverified projections and a32-read concurrency bound. Rebuilt successfully against prepared release2026.10.26 main46fd91415 without product conflicts. Final exact-head hosted coverage and review remain merge prerequisites, distinct from the earlier complete local100percent run."
  "2026-10-26T05:50:24.682Z","harness:codex","PR1596 second full review found a valid failed-read atomicity defect in the shared authoritative fallback cache. Native regression warms two real history streams, appends to the first sorted stream, corrupts the second, observes strict refusal, then reads only the valid stream: unchanged783318c3b omits the appended event. Stage stream updates and deletions in a local Map and publish it only after every selected read succeeds. The existing closure is preserved as immutable history; only this canonical item is reopened and claimed for the refinement."
  "2026-10-26T06:01:02.512Z","harness:codex","The full static pipeline passed source/dependency/contracts, tracker readiness, registry, SDK surface and10entrypoint import costs, then failed the existing qualified CLI transport gate: get best497ms above362, list502 above419, context481 above433. Control medians66/39ms qualify the runner; this is retained as a genuine failed product-budget verdict and no cause is asserted. Repeat the identical gate alone once, preserving every bound, before the unchanged graph/record/mutation suffix. Full source coverage before the atomic-cache refinement passed11447tests at exact100percent across all four dimensions; final hosted source coverage remains required after the refinement."
  "2026-10-26T06:04:18.756Z","harness:codex","Final atomic-cache refinement:121 focused native tests pass, including the unchanged-code failure reproduced before staging stream updates locally. All TypeScript targets, build and workflow permissions pass. Full static passed every stage across the original run and the identical isolated transport retry plus canonical graph/record/mutation suffix; the earlier qualified timing failure is retained and no threshold was changed. Linked tests now pass again. The final reviewed head must independently pass hosted exact100percent coverage; earlier complete local11447-test proof is explicitly before this atomic-cache change."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T00:06:30.630Z","harness:codex","Integrity cost boundary: default cache freshness hashes complete selected authoritative streams. Explicit item filters bound that population; strict verification additionally replays each selected stream before all other filters. Full-history raw timestamps remain sealed values in verified entries while ordering uses normalized timestamps. Performance documentation was corrected rather than claiming O(delta) source validation."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T01:24:47.928Z","harness:codex","A history projection cannot authenticate earlier records from byte length or the final record hash. Bind rows to a digest of the same complete raw stream, explicitly distinguish unverified reads, and verify selected authoritative chains before filters or pagination can hide corruption."
  "2026-10-26T04:54:56.263Z","harness:codex","For review rework use pm item reopen <id> <reason> --expected-result <current outcome>, then claim --start. Reopening deliberately archives prior closure expectations; the shipped planning-recovery contract preserves an explicitly supplied new expectation. Restore active readiness before running assurance and do not reopen its completed recovery owner as an unresolved feature."
